<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>闲聊 on 编程那些事儿</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E9%97%B2%E8%81%8A/</link><description>Recent content in 闲聊 on 编程那些事儿</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>zh-cn</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:31:03 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E9%97%B2%E8%81%8A/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>寒暄与闲聊</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/life/small-talk/</link><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:25:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/life/small-talk/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;在美国，&lt;strong&gt;跟陌生人搭话是日常礼貌，不是套近乎&lt;/strong&gt;。电梯里、排队时、等咖啡时，旁边的人可能随口来一句 &lt;code&gt;Crazy weather today, huh?&lt;/code&gt;——这时候不接话，会被理解成不友好。&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>